SEL: PEAT can pull SEL relays behind a SEL RTAC through the RTAC's engineering access tunnels (access points, and the SEL server's ``WHO`` and ``PORT n``), over Telnet, raw TCP, TLS, or SSH. The paths are configured with the new ``sel.rtac_tunnels`` option or ``peat pull -d selrelay --rtac-tunnel``, or come from a pulled RTAC with ``sel.rtac_pull_downstream``. This is off by default, read-only (at access level 1 by default, with the settings from ``SHO``), one session at a time, and each RTAC login is tried once per RTAC; direct routes need ``sel.allow_direct_tunnels``, and file transfers ``sel.tunnel_file_transfer``.
